# Vacuum Frequency Theory

## A Geometric Gauge Conjecture Derived from Tetryonic Proton Topology

**James M. Moore**
Based on the Tetryonic geometric framework of Kelvin C. Abraham (*Principa Geometrica*)
Articulated with the assistance of ChatGPT 5.5
May 2026

---

# Abstract

Vacuum Frequency Theory proposes that electromagnetic propagation possesses a fundamental geometric gauge determined by equilateral proton topology.

Within the Tetryonic framework introduced by Kelvin C. Abraham, the proton is modeled not as a sphere but as a tetrahedral geometric structure composed of equilateral triangular faces. The orthographic projection of this topology produces a regular hexagonal geometry whose circumscribed radius naturally implies a unique equilateral face altitude:

[
\lambda_q = 1\times10^{-15},\mathrm{m}
]

This gauge length generates a corresponding vacuum propagation frequency:

[
\nu_{\mathrm{vac}}
==================

# \frac{c}{\lambda_q}

2.99792458\times10^{23},\mathrm{Hz}
]

designated the **Vacuum Frequency**.

The theory further proposes that electromagnetic quanta are composed of invariant equilateral gauge domains rather than arbitrarily shrinking point-like structures, and that higher-energy quanta correspond to increasing superposition density over fixed geometric area.

This work presents the axioms, theorem structure, geometric derivation, physical conjectures, and required experimental tests necessary to evaluate or falsify the theory.

---

# Part I — Foundational Axioms

# Axiom 1 — Geometric Existence

Physical structure is fundamentally geometric rather than point-like.

All stable electromagnetic structure arises from invariant geometric relations.

---

# Axiom 2 — Equilateral Gauge Symmetry

The fundamental electromagnetic gauge domain is equilateral.

Its characteristic area is invariant under propagation:

[
A_q=\frac{\lambda_q^2}{\sqrt3}
]

where:

[
\lambda_q
=========

1\times10^{-15},\mathrm{m}
]

---

# Axiom 3 — Tetrahedral Proton Topology

The proton possesses tetrahedral geometric topology composed of equilateral triangular gauge faces.

The proton is therefore anisotropic rather than perfectly spherical.

---

# Axiom 4 — Orthographic Hexagonal Projection

The orthographic Z-axis projection of the tetrahedral proton produces a regular hexagonal cross-section.

The circumscribed radius of this projection equals the side-length of the equilateral gauge face.

---

# Axiom 5 — Geometric Gauge Determination

The proton topology determines the electromagnetic gauge scale through Euclidean equilateral geometry.

The gauge length is not arbitrary.

It is a geometric consequence of proton topology.

---

# Axiom 6 — Fixed Gauge Domains

Electromagnetic quanta do not shrink indefinitely with increasing energy.

Higher-energy states correspond instead to increased excitation density or superposition over invariant gauge domains.

---

# Axiom 7 — Vacuum Propagation

Electromagnetic propagation through vacuum occurs at a fixed geometric propagation rate:

[
c=\lambda_q\nu_{\mathrm{vac}}
]

where:

[
\nu_{\mathrm{vac}}
==================

2.99792458\times10^{23},\mathrm{Hz}
]

is designated the Vacuum Frequency.

