# Part IV — Required Experimental Verification

# Requirement 1 — Proton Anisotropy

High-energy scattering experiments must determine whether the proton exhibits orientation-dependent geometric structure inconsistent with exact spherical symmetry.

Evidence of tetrahedral or hexagonal anisotropy would strongly support the theory.

---

# Requirement 2 — Multiple Proton Radii

Independent proton radius measurements must determine whether distinct experiments probe different geometric radii rather than a single spherical boundary.

---

# Requirement 3 — Gauge Resonance Structure

